insert into public.chapters (id, story_id, number, title, body, status, published_at, created_at) values
  ('f131b3ae-a6a0-55f7-a272-7bb5ec1ebf7e', '7a307cbd-2824-5884-aaf7-5b89bb6edbb7', 1, 'Step Four Hundred and Twelve', 'Song Ping had swept the steps of Cloudy Peak every morning for a thousand years. There were nine hundred and ninety-nine steps. He knew each one. He had names for the crooked ones.

The sect had been empty for eight hundred years, give or take. Song Ping was not entirely sure, because he had stopped counting somewhere around the fourth century, when it became depressing.

He was sweeping step four hundred and twelve, the one he called Grumpy, when a small, muddy girl in a torn disciple''s robe crawled over the top of the cliff, saw him, and burst into tears.

''Please,'' she sobbed. ''Is this a sect? Can I join? I''ll sweep. I''m very good at sweeping.''

Song Ping looked at his broom. Then he looked at her. ''Oh dear,'' he said.

Clouds rolled across Cloudy Peak''s abandoned courtyards, and the bells in the empty towers swayed without ringing.

Little Mei said, "Master Song, the manual says forming a core takes ten years. You did it before breakfast?"

That evening, a sword light streaked across the sky toward Cloudy Peak, carrying the emblem of a rival sect.', 'published', now() - interval '111.804 days', now() - interval '111.804 days'),
  ('fe424c2b-5e98-5a0f-aaf5-3af18e4418b2', '7a307cbd-2824-5884-aaf7-5b89bb6edbb7', 2, 'Waiting at the Gate', 'In which Song Ping explains his master told him to wait at the gate and never returned. Mei asks to become a disciple, and he has no idea how to say no.

Mountain wind carried the scent of pine and snow, and the peaks beyond stood silent and patient as old monks.

For the first time in a thousand years, the sect felt like a sect. It was mostly the noise.

"Master Song, the manual says forming a core takes ten years. You did it before breakfast?" Little Mei said.

Moss grew between the flagstones of the training ground, except along one perfectly swept path.

Teaching, it turned out, was much harder than defeating a calamity-level beast. Beasts did not ask why.

Little Mei came back from the market with news: the outside world believed Cloudy Peak was a forbidden ruin, guarded by a monster.', 'published', now() - interval '108.433 days', now() - interval '108.433 days'),
  ('6677fd38-2e23-506e-a494-6353c1d7c290', '7a307cbd-2824-5884-aaf7-5b89bb6edbb7', 3, 'Apprentices Can''t Teach', 'In which Song Ping insists apprentices cannot take disciples, so he teaches Mei ''unofficially'', starting with sweeping and breathing exercises.

Clouds rolled across Cloudy Peak''s abandoned courtyards, and the bells in the empty towers swayed without ringing.

He kept looking for his master''s footprints on the path. He had been doing it for so long it had become a habit, like breathing.

"My master said to wait at the gate. I''ve been very good at waiting. It''s the only thing I''m sure I''m good at," Song Ping said.

In the Scripture Hall, a thousand years of manuals lay stacked in perfect order, dusted daily by one very bored apprentice.

For the first time in a thousand years, the sect felt like a sect. It was mostly the noise.

Little Mei said, "Master Song, the manual says forming a core takes ten years. You did it before breakfast?"

Song Ping swept the steps the next morning and found a footprint that was not his, and not Mei''s.', 'published', now() - interval '104.982 days', now() - interval '104.982 days'),
  ('62652260-345d-5189-a3d7-793cfb1ebb8d', '7a307cbd-2824-5884-aaf7-5b89bb6edbb7', 4, 'Basic Breathing', 'In which Song Ping''s ''basic'' breathing exercise is a forgotten heaven-tier technique. Mei nearly passes out and opens three meridians in a day.

Mountain wind carried the scent of pine and snow, and the peaks beyond stood silent and patient as old monks.

Song Ping had never been told he was strong. Nobody had been around to tell him anything for eight centuries.

