insert into public.chapters (id, story_id, number, title, body, status, published_at, created_at) values
  ('8a300d96-cefc-542e-a84f-6c8a189d73d1', '8d17853b-57c5-5d68-a337-45a575609c90', 1, 'Floor Three Delivery', 'Dayo Adebayo delivered jollof rice to the Tower''s lower floors six days a week, on a scooter with a dented box and a horn that only worked when it felt like it. The adventurers on floor three tipped well, mostly because the goblins on floor three tended to eat couriers who didn''t arrive on time.

He was halfway across the floor-three bridge, balancing four orders and a bag of puff-puff, when the air turned blue and the System spoke for the first time in his life.

[ERROR. CLASS ASSIGNMENT FAILED. ASSIGNING DEFAULT: ERROR.]

[CLASS: ERROR. LEVEL: 1. SKILLS: ???]

The puff-puff bag split. Dayo watched the little golden balls bounce across the bridge toward a very interested goblin, and thought, distinctly: my customers are going to be so upset.

The Tower rose over the lagoon like a needle of black glass, its upper floors lost in cloud.

"Your class is literally called Error and you''re still alive. I''m starting to think that''s the skill," Funmi said.

[ERROR. ERROR. ERROR. FLOOR 61 ACCESS: UNLOCKED?]', 'published', now() - interval '99.736 days', now() - interval '99.736 days'),
  ('8d1411ac-bd01-5610-a5d8-deee2de831fe', '8d17853b-57c5-5d68-a337-45a575609c90', 2, 'Skills: ???', 'In which Dayo''s skills are hidden. He discovers his first by accident: [Clip], letting him walk through a wall that should be solid.

Guild banners hung from the floor-ten plaza, each one marking the highest floor that guild had ever cleared.

Whatever he was, the Tower had noticed. Floors he''d never visited had started rearranging themselves when he arrived.

Funmi said, "Your class is literally called Error and you''re still alive. I''m starting to think that''s the skill."

Floor markets bustled at the Tower''s base, selling potions, maps and suya to adventurers before their climbs.

Every skill he unlocked made the System''s text glitch a little more. He was beginning to suspect it was trying to fix him.

[ERROR. ERROR. ERROR. FLOOR 61 ACCESS: UNLOCKED?]', 'published', now() - interval '97.249 days', now() - interval '97.249 days'),
  ('4321033b-b276-5254-a96e-f92f2d0bf645', '8d17853b-57c5-5d68-a337-45a575609c90', 3, 'Funmi', 'In which Dayo meets Funmi, a [Cartographer] whose maps of the Tower are the best in Lagos. She wants to know how he got through her wall.

The Tower rose over the lagoon like a needle of black glass, its upper floors lost in cloud.

The guilds treated the Tower like a war. Dayo kept treating it like a city, and it kept working.

Funmi said, "You keep finding shortcuts nobody else can see. Do you know how annoying that is to a mapmaker?"

Blue System text flickered at the edge of Dayo''s vision, occasionally showing characters that did not belong to any language.

Whatever he was, the Tower had noticed. Floors he''d never visited had started rearranging themselves when he arrived.

When Dayo checked his status window that night, a new line had appeared: [Administrator privileges: 0.01%].', 'published', now() - interval '94.832 days', now() - interval '94.832 days'),
  ('95c53f65-9d6a-5533-a6fe-3f6c0ec0a83a', '8d17853b-57c5-5d68-a337-45a575609c90', 4, 'Shortcuts', 'In which using [Clip], Dayo finds shortcuts between floors that should not connect. Funmi maps them, fascinated and furious.

Guild banners hung from the floor-ten plaza, each one marking the highest floor that guild had ever cleared.

Dayo had spent his life getting things where they needed to go. Climbing, he decided, was just a very vertical delivery.

"Every guild wants to know what you are. I just want to know why the System is scared of you," Kestrel said.

Floor markets bustled at the Tower''s base, selling potions, maps and suya to adventurers before their climbs.

The guilds treated the Tower like a war. Dayo kept treating it like a city, and it kept working.

Funmi said, "You keep finding shortcuts nobody else can see. Do you know how annoying that is to a mapmaker?"

His phone buzzed with a delivery order. The address was floor one hundred.', 'published', now() - interval '92.132 days', now() - interval '92.132 days'),
  ('f3ac26d1-b11f-5677-a161-c9876824bbee', '8d17853b-57c5-5d68-a337-45a575609c90', 5, 'Guild Recruiters', 'In which word spreads about the courier with the impossible class. Recruiters from every guild crowd his mother''s closed shop.

The Tower rose over the lagoon like a needle of black glass, its upper floors lost in cloud.

He didn''t want a wish. He wanted his mother''s shop back. A wish would probably cover that.

Kestrel said, "Nobody''s reached floor sixty-one in four years. Maybe the Tower doesn''t want anyone to."

Blue System text flickered at the edge of Dayo''s vision, occasionally showing characters that did not belong to any language.

Dayo had spent his life getting things where they needed to go. Climbing, he decided, was just a very vertical delivery.

The guild ranking board updated at dawn, and Dayo''s name was on it, at a rank that did not exist.', 'published', now() - interval '89.507 days', now() - interval '89.507 days'),
  ('7f8bce3c-cff3-5971-af0f-4093892a302a', '8d17853b-57c5-5d68-a337-45a575609c90', 6, 'Guildmaster Aro', 'In which Guildmaster Aro of the Iron Crown, the strongest guild, offers Dayo a contract. Dayo reads the fine print and says no.

Guild banners hung from the floor-ten plaza, each one marking the highest floor that guild had ever cleared.

Every skill he unlocked made the System''s text glitch a little more. He was beginning to suspect it was trying to fix him.

"The Tower rewards order." Guildmaster Aro paused. "Classes, ranks, rules. You, courier, are a rounding error."

Floor markets bustled at the Tower''s base, selling potions, maps and suya to adventurers before their climbs.

He didn''t want a wish. He wanted his mother''s shop back. A wish would probably cover that.

Somewhere on floor forty, a boss that had never moved before opened its eyes and turned toward the stairs.', 'published', now() - interval '87.202 days', now() - interval '87.202 days'),
