  ('e53e389e-10a7-582d-a6ef-26b885c7024f', 'cfefaaff-f064-5e08-a2c1-20ae2192cb6d', 20, 'Out', 'In which The house''s outer door opens onto an ordinary street at dawn. The survivors walk out and do not look at each other.

Air vents breathed softly in the ceiling, cold and faintly sweet, like a hospital at night.

She counted the hours. She counted the doors. She tried very hard not to count the people.

