White light came from nowhere in particular and cast no shadows, so every room looked like the inside of an eggshell.

Iris had spent ten years making decisions in the back of moving ambulances. She had never had this long to think about one.

The inquiry reopened six weeks later. Iris testified for four hours. She told them everything, including the parts that would cost her the job, and they did.

She works at a free clinic now, in a building with a great many windows. Sometimes patients ask why every room has a clock that runs exactly on time, and she says it''s a small thing that matters to her, and leaves it at that.', 'published', now() - interval '38.798 days', now() - interval '38.798 days')
