insert into public.chapters (id, story_id, number, title, body, status, published_at, created_at) values
  ('10d7b675-7d4f-50e6-a888-6e9648a755a4', '6970c36d-a4d0-5de4-ab4d-beef4b5e228c', 1, 'Hero''s Homework', 'Hikari Mizuno had saved the Kingdom of Aldermere from a dragon, a lich and one very rude archduke, and the worst thing about coming home was the maths test on Monday.

It wasn''t that she had forgotten maths. It was that, during her year away, she had learned to calculate a fireball''s trajectory in her head under pressure, and her school still wanted her to show her working.

She was rehearsing her excuse for the missing homework when Sora Amano slid into the seat beside her, smelling faintly of sulphur, and said, without looking up: ''You''re late, Mizuno. Did you get lost? Again?''

Hikari froze. Nobody else in this world knew she had been lost for a year.

Cherry blossoms drifted past the classroom window and stuck to the glass like confetti from a celebration nobody had invited them to.

"I''m tutoring the Demon King in calculus." Sora paused. "Please don''t tell anyone. It''s embarrassing for both of us."

That night a summoning circle glowed on Hikari''s bedroom floor, and the voice inside it said: ''Hero, we need you. Bring the tutor.''', 'published', now() - interval '1.984 days', now() - interval '1.984 days'),
  ('d5b9feda-f54a-5692-abfc-edc088a34cd2', '6970c36d-a4d0-5de4-ab4d-beef4b5e228c', 2, 'The Demon King''s Tutor', 'In which Sora confesses he was summoned too: as the Demon King''s maths tutor. He came back the same day she did.

After school the clubroom filled with orange evening light and the sound of someone practising trumpet badly two floors down.

She was beginning to suspect that being summoned twice was not a coincidence. Nothing about Sora ever was.

Sora said, "I''m tutoring the Demon King in calculus. Please don''t tell anyone. It''s embarrassing for both of us."

The school corridors smelled of floor wax, instant noodles and the faint nervous energy of exam week.

She had been a hero for a year. She was finding it surprisingly difficult to be a normal seventeen-year-old.

Demon King Valdris said, "Your Sora is a cruel and terrible teacher. I have improved by forty percent. I resent this."

That night a summoning circle glowed on Hikari''s bedroom floor, and the voice inside it said: ''Hero, we need you. Bring the tutor.''', 'published', now() - interval '1.643 days', now() - interval '1.643 days'),
  ('f4a9ad44-4c63-5f81-ac31-0e5b2d4387bf', '6970c36d-a4d0-5de4-ab4d-beef4b5e228c', 3, 'Truce', 'In which Hikari and Sora agree to a truce to keep each other''s secrets, while continuing to compete for top of the class.

Cherry blossoms drifted past the classroom window and stuck to the glass like confetti from a celebration nobody had invited them to.

Every time Sora mentioned the Demon King, Hikari felt a strange, sharp pang she refused to call jealousy.

"You saved a kingdom and you still can''t do quadratics." Sora paused. "Impressive, really."

Rain pattered against the convenience store awning, and the warm light inside made the street look like a painting.

She was beginning to suspect that being summoned twice was not a coincidence. Nothing about Sora ever was.

"I''m tutoring the Demon King in calculus." Sora paused. "Please don''t tell anyone. It''s embarrassing for both of us."

The class rankings were posted, and for the first time, Hikari and Sora were tied.', 'published', now() - interval '1.839 days', now() - interval '1.839 days'),
  ('e68ad871-02f0-5ef2-aa70-7766be0d34ad', '6970c36d-a4d0-5de4-ab4d-beef4b5e228c', 4, 'Yuki', 'In which their best friend Yuki notices both of them acting strangely and decides they must be secretly dating.

After school the clubroom filled with orange evening light and the sound of someone practising trumpet badly two floors down.

Hikari had faced a dragon without blinking. Facing Sora''s smug little smile across a desk was somehow harder.

"You two argue like an old married couple. A married couple who might stab each other," Yuki said.

The school corridors smelled of floor wax, instant noodles and the faint nervous energy of exam week.

Every time Sora mentioned the Demon King, Hikari felt a strange, sharp pang she refused to call jealousy.

"You saved a kingdom and you still can''t do quadratics. Impressive, really," Sora said.

That night a summoning circle glowed on Hikari''s bedroom floor, and the voice inside it said: ''Hero, we need you. Bring the tutor.''', 'published', now() - interval '1.768 days', now() - interval '1.768 days'),
  ('5faf50c2-9bb9-5743-a84c-745eaa66f6c0', '6970c36d-a4d0-5de4-ab4d-beef4b5e228c', 5, 'The Summoning Circle', 'In which a summoning circle appears in Hikari''s room. Aldermere needs its hero again, and the summons insists she bring the tutor.

Cherry blossoms drifted past the classroom window and stuck to the glass like confetti from a celebration nobody had invited them to.

Aldermere had taught her to fight. Nobody had taught her what to do with a rival who kept being kind at the worst moments.

"Is anyone going to tell me why you both keep checking the sky like it owes you money?" Yuki said quietly.

Rain pattered against the convenience store awning, and the warm light inside made the street look like a painting.

Hikari had faced a dragon without blinking. Facing Sora''s smug little smile across a desk was somehow harder.

On the rooftop, Sora was standing at the edge, looking at the sky, and he did not hear her come up the stairs.', 'published', now() - interval '1.464 days', now() - interval '1.464 days'),
