"Is anyone going to tell me why you both keep checking the sky like it owes you money?" Yuki said.

In the morning, the Demon King was sitting in the back row of their class, wearing a school uniform two sizes too small.', 'published', now() - interval '0.050 days', now() - interval '0.050 days'),
  ('b5ec63f3-881f-5ee9-a7c8-c7b356e7d950', '6970c36d-a4d0-5de4-ab4d-beef4b5e228c', 27, 'Fireworks', 'In which under the fireworks, Hikari and Sora agree on a new contest: who can be the better partner. Both of them intend to win.

Cherry blossoms drifted past the classroom window and stuck to the glass like confetti from a celebration nobody had invited them to.

She was beginning to suspect that being summoned twice was not a coincidence. Nothing about Sora ever was.

"I''m tutoring the Demon King in calculus. Please don''t tell anyone. It''s embarrassing for both of us," Sora said.

Rain pattered against the convenience store awning, and the warm light inside made the street look like a painting.

She had been a hero for a year. She was finding it surprisingly difficult to be a normal seventeen-year-old.

"Your Sora is a cruel and terrible teacher." Demon King Valdris paused. "I have improved by forty percent. I resent this."

That night a summoning circle glowed on Hikari''s bedroom floor, and the voice inside it said: ''Hero, we need you. Bring the tutor.''', 'published', now() - interval '0.050 days', now() - interval '0.050 days'),
  ('6b490c94-261c-5ce6-a050-e6676f574230', '6970c36d-a4d0-5de4-ab4d-beef4b5e228c', 28, 'Summoned Again', 'In which a new summoning circle appears on Hikari''s floor, glowing brighter than ever. This time, it is asking for both of them by name.

After school the clubroom filled with orange evening light and the sound of someone practising trumpet badly two floors down.

Every time Sora mentioned the Demon King, Hikari felt a strange, sharp pang she refused to call jealousy.

Sora said, "You saved a kingdom and you still can''t do quadratics. Impressive, really."

The school corridors smelled of floor wax, instant noodles and the faint nervous energy of exam week.

She was beginning to suspect that being summoned twice was not a coincidence. Nothing about Sora ever was.

Sora said, "I''m tutoring the Demon King in calculus. Please don''t tell anyone. It''s embarrassing for both of us."

