A buyer''s offer arrived, generous and final, with a deadline at the end of the month.', 'published', now() - interval '37.414 days', now() - interval '37.414 days'),
  ('eca68369-817a-5deb-a991-c1d4357a0204', '054b855b-86c2-50d2-a240-01ecd72ce88f', 19, 'One Farm', 'In which Chioma and Erik decide to take down the fence between the halves and run the farm as one, the way it was meant to be.

The river ran slow and brown around the bend, carrying willow leaves and the occasional startled duck.

Chioma had built a life in the city that never needed this farm. She was beginning to suspect she had built it that way on purpose.

"Twenty years of silence over one flood. Both families stubborn as river stones," Aunt Ngozi said.

Rain drummed on the barn roof, and the old horses shifted in their stalls and blew softly through their noses.

Erik had changed and not changed. It was the not-changed parts that kept catching her off guard.

In the attic, behind a loose board, Chioma found a bundle of letters in her father''s handwriting, addressed to Mr Lindgren and never sent.', 'published', now() - interval '33.848 days', now() - interval '33.848 days'),
  ('d854c22d-be60-5f07-a022-0971e42fc181', '054b855b-86c2-50d2-a240-01ecd72ce88f', 20, 'Harvest', 'In which the first joint harvest in twenty years comes in. Both families, and half the village, gather for the harvest supper.

