  ('a6ecc51a-7a8a-5b57-a609-5506e7fc7516', '054b855b-86c2-50d2-a240-01ecd72ce88f', 22, 'Where the River Bends', 'In which under the willow at sunset, Erik asks whether the promise they made at twelve still counts. Chioma says it never stopped counting.

Evening light turned the river gold, and swallows skimmed the water for insects in long, looping arcs.

The flood had taken the crops, the barn and both families'' trust. Chioma was starting to wonder which loss had been the worst.

"I mended the gate every year." Erik paused. "Just in case anyone came back to use it."

